  "generated_text": ".. **Identify the composition of functions**: We are given $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$. This means $f(x) = q(p(r(x)))$.\n\n2. **Find the inverse of the composition**: To find $f^{-1}$, we need to reverse the order of the functions. This is because the inverse of a composition of functions is the composition of the inverses in reverse order.\n\n3. **Apply the inverse functions**: The inverse of $f(x) = q(p(r(x)))$ is $f^{-1}(x) = r^{-1}(p^{-1}(q^{-1}(x)))$.\n\n4. **Choose the correct expression**: The correct expression for $f^{-1}$ is $r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}$, which corresponds to choice C.\n\n5. **Conclusion**: The final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.\nThe answer answer is C",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[c, 'C']",
    "gold_answer": "Let $y = f(x) = q(p(r(x))).$  Applying $q^{-1},$ we get\n\\[q^{-1}(y) = p(r(x)).\\]Applying $p^{-1},$ we get\n\\[p^{-1}(q^{-1}(y)) = r(x).\\]Finally, applying $r^{-1}(x),$ we get\n\\[r^{-1}(p^{-1}(q^{-1}(y))) = x.\\]Hence, $f^{-1} = r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}.$  The correct answer is $\\boxed{\\text{C}}.$",
    "is_correct": true
